WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:08.840
And now we come to a very important part where we can understand how the partitions are really improving

00:08.840 --> 00:10.240
the performance of my query.

00:10.240 --> 00:13.280
And of course, we can do that by checking the execution plan.

00:13.320 --> 00:18.120
So now in order to compare like the behavior with and without a partition, what we have to do is to

00:18.160 --> 00:20.440
create a mirror table without partition.

00:20.440 --> 00:22.560
So we have our table here, the partition one.

00:22.560 --> 00:28.320
What I'm just going to do, I will go over here and say into and we're going to call it sales orders

00:28.640 --> 00:30.600
underscore no partition.

00:31.520 --> 00:35.720
So we are taking the data and the structure from the orders partitions.

00:35.720 --> 00:37.880
And of course it will not be partitioned.

00:38.080 --> 00:39.960
So let's go and execute it.

00:40.000 --> 00:43.760
Now if you go over here we can see that we have two tables.

00:43.760 --> 00:46.000
We have the no partition and the partition one.

00:46.000 --> 00:49.960
So now what we're going to do, we're going to write a query on both tables and then compare the execution

00:49.960 --> 00:50.440
plan.

00:50.480 --> 00:52.640
So first let's start with the no partition.

00:53.000 --> 00:58.680
So from and now in order to see the effect of the partition what we're going to do we're going to say

00:58.840 --> 01:01.680
where order dates equal to.

01:01.720 --> 01:06.040
And now we're just going to pick a value like 2026 the 1st of January.

01:06.040 --> 01:07.840
So let's go and query it.

01:07.880 --> 01:12.240
And we're going to do the same thing a new query but this time for the partitions.

01:12.300 --> 01:12.780
So.

01:14.940 --> 01:18.460
Now in order to see the execution plan, make sure to activate it.

01:18.460 --> 01:23.100
So we go to the action bar over here and we're going to say include the actual execution plan.

01:23.100 --> 01:25.460
So let's click on it and execute.

01:25.460 --> 01:27.820
And with that we have here an execution plan.

01:27.860 --> 01:30.540
And let's do the same thing for the node partitions.

01:30.580 --> 01:31.700
So execute.

01:31.740 --> 01:33.740
And we have here execution plan.

01:33.740 --> 01:35.860
So now let's check what do we have in the execution plan.

01:35.900 --> 01:37.540
We're going to focus on this one over here.

01:37.540 --> 01:40.260
So right click on it and then go to properties.

01:40.300 --> 01:42.900
And now we can see a lot of details about the execution plan.

01:42.940 --> 01:45.500
But what is interesting is the number of rows.

01:45.740 --> 01:47.540
So as you can see we are reading four rows.

01:47.580 --> 01:48.900
That means the whole table.

01:48.940 --> 01:51.980
And of course we have here the CPU and the other costs.

01:52.020 --> 01:54.180
Now let's go and check the partition.

01:54.180 --> 01:55.580
So let's click over here.

01:55.580 --> 02:00.060
So now if you check over here you can see that the total number of rows is one.

02:00.060 --> 02:02.580
So SQL didn't read all four rows.

02:02.620 --> 02:03.900
It reads only row.

02:03.940 --> 02:06.500
And that's because we have in this partition only one row.

02:06.540 --> 02:10.620
And as you can see the number of partitions that is used is as well only one.

02:10.620 --> 02:16.580
So as you can see using partition we have reduced the number of rows that is retrieved from the files.

02:16.660 --> 02:22.300
Now let's go and retrieve like two data from two different partitions and check the execution plan.

02:22.860 --> 02:26.760
So let's target 2025 the last day of the year.

02:26.760 --> 02:27.560
Like this.

02:27.560 --> 02:29.800
So let's go and execute it.

02:29.920 --> 02:32.160
And the same thing for the other query.

02:34.560 --> 02:36.800
So let's check the without partition.

02:37.280 --> 02:39.600
We still we are reading like four rows.

02:39.640 --> 02:45.640
But now if you go to the other one, if you check the execution plan and check the table scan, you

02:45.640 --> 02:51.200
can see we are reading only two rows, and this time the number of partitions that are involved in this

02:51.200 --> 02:52.200
query is two.

02:52.240 --> 02:55.640
And that's because we have partition for 2025 and 2026.

02:55.640 --> 02:57.280
So as you can see it's worth the efforts.

02:57.320 --> 02:59.120
We have optimized our queries.

02:59.120 --> 03:02.400
And this has a great impact on bigtable's.

03:02.400 --> 03:06.480
The number of resources and the number of reads can be reduced massively.

03:06.520 --> 03:07.240
All right my friends.

03:07.240 --> 03:09.280
So that's all about the partitions in SQL.

03:09.320 --> 03:10.120
It is amazing.

03:10.120 --> 03:15.280
And you can use it as well not only in databases but as well in many other data platforms and tools

03:15.280 --> 03:18.800
where you always can divide your data in order to optimize the performance.

